cbt-407-409.l4:811:1-86:
  "You, Carl Elias Moses, are charged that you, on or about 23 October 1989, at the premises of Trans-Pacific Credit Pte Ltd, Singapore, being an employee, and in such capacity being entrusted by Trans-Pacific Credit Pte Ltd (“the company”) with property, namely, the proceeds of the sale of 2,000 Overseas Union Bank Warrant 1994 received by you from DBS Securities Pte Ltd pursuant to a sale (per contract number 414270/501) of the said warrants, for the purpose of paying the same to the company, did dishonestly misappropriate the said proceeds, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 408 of the Penal Code 1871."
cbt-407-409.l4:812:1-85:
  "You, Carl Elias Moses, are charged that you, on or about 23 October 1989, at the premises of Trans-Pacific Credit Pte Ltd, Singapore, being a director of a corporation, and in such capacity being entrusted by Trans-Pacific Credit Pte Ltd (“the company”) with property, namely, the proceeds of the sale of 2,000 Overseas Union Bank Warrant 1994 received by you from DBS Securities Pte Ltd pursuant to a sale (per contract number 414270/501) of the said warrants, for the purpose of paying the same to the company, did dishonestly misappropriate the said proceeds, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 409 of the Penal Code 1871."
cbt-407-409.l4:813:1-96:
  "A charge under section 408 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of criminal breach of trust by an employee (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: being in any manner entrusted IN THAT CAPACITY with the property, or with any dominion over it — it is not enough that a person who happened to be an employee was entrusted."
cbt-407-409.l4:814:1-79:
  "You, A, are charged that you, on or about a date unknown, at A's warehouse, Singapore, the property hereinafter mentioned having been entrusted to you for the purpose of storage for rent or charge, and being entrusted by one Z with property, namely, the furniture of the said Z under a contract that it shall be returned on payment of a stipulated sum for warehouse room, did dishonestly dispose of the said furniture in violation of a legal contract, express or implied, which you had made touching the discharge of the said trust, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 407 of the Penal Code 1871."
cbt-407-409.l4:815:1-83:
  "You, A, are charged that you, on or about a date unknown, at A's place of business, Singapore, in the way of your business as an agent, and in such capacity being entrusted by one Z of Penang with property, namely, $5,000 remitted to you by the said Z with directions to you to invest the same in Government securities, pursuant to an express or implied contract between you and the said Z that all sums remitted by the said Z to you shall be invested by you according to his direction, did dishonestly use the said moneys in violation of a legal contract, express or implied, which you had made touching the discharge of the said trust, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 409 of the Penal Code 1871."
cbt-407-409.l4:816:1-111:
  "A charge under section 409 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of criminal breach of trust by a public servant, or by a banker, merchant, agent, director, officer, partner, key executive or fiduciary (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: being entrusted with the property, or with dominion over it, in one of the capacities section 409(1) names — (a) as a public servant; (b) in the way of a trade, profession or business as a banker, merchant, factor, broker, attorney or agent; (c) in a professional capacity OTHER than one of those; (d) as a director of a corporation; (e) as an officer of an unincorporated association; (f) as a partner in a partnership; (g) as a key executive of a corporation, an unincorporated association or a partnership; or (h) as a fiduciary."
